  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "A landlord shall apply a rent deposit that a tenant has paid to the landlord or to a former landlord in payment of the rent for the last rent period before the tenancy terminates.",
  "reason": "Under subsection 106(10) of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006, a rent deposit can only be applied in payment of the rent for the last rent period before the tenancy terminates. Because the clause allows the landlord to apply the deposit to utility bills and cleaning costs instead, it contradicts the Act and is void under section 4."
}

